From 2ad27602d827e41cb6ebb688283fa847a79eb5fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Correa da Silva Sanches <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Mar 2026 12:40:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] kn5000: Add tone generator device (IC303) with PCM
 waveform playback

New kn5000_tonegen_device implements the TC183C230002 custom tone generator:
- Register-indirect interface (addr latch at 0x100000, data at 0x100002)
- 64 voice states with 28 registers each (7 groups x 4 banks)
- 13 global configuration registers
- Voice control state machine (key on/off)
- PCM waveform reading from IC304-IC307 ROM region (16MB)
- Stereo 48kHz sound stream output
- Keybed event queue (replaces old HLE queue in driver)

Replaces the previous stub (noprw at 0x100000) with a proper device that
accepts firmware register writes and produces audio output. The SubCPU
firmware's 2,317 register writes during ToneGen_Config_Init are now
processed by the device.

IC304-IC306 remain NO_DUMP but synthetic approximations (sine, sawtooth,
square/triangle) can be placed in the ROM path for basic audio.
